    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "For the spinor representations, since Spin is a subspace of the even Cliﬀord algebra, we only need to look at table 2.2, which implies that the number of irreducible inequivalent spinor representations is"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
